
  [1mFiles.[0m [38;5;153msrc/logger/core.js[39m — pure, no I/O, no runtime detection. [38;5;153msrc/logger/node.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/logger/browser.js[39m — thin
  adapters. Each gets a five-line dual-mode tail ([38;5;153mmodule.exports[39m if present, else a [38;5;153mwindow.__logger*[39m global), so Node
  requires the adapter directly and [38;5;153mindex.html[39m loads [38;5;153mcore.js[39m then [38;5;153mbrowser.js[39m as two ordered [38;5;153m<script>[39m tags before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m.

  [1mCall-site API[0m — five levels, one shape:

  logger.[33mdebug[39m(msg, ctx)   [32m// msg: static string, ctx: flat object[39m
  logger.[33minfo[39m(msg, ctx)
  logger.[33mwarn[39m(msg, ctx)
  logger.[33merror[39m(msg, ctx)   [32m// ctx.err may carry an Error[39m
  logger.[33mfatal[39m(msg, ctx)

  No [38;5;153mchild()[39m loggers, no formatters, no custom levels — YAGNI until something needs them.

  [1mRecord model[0m (this is the wire format, so it's the expensive part to change later):

  { [36mv[39m: [32m1[39m, [36mts[39m: [31m"2026-09-17T10:38:21.123Z"[39m, [36mlevel[39m: [31m"warn"[39m, [36mmsg[39m: [31m"..."[39m,
    [36mctx[39m: { ... }, [36merr[39m: { name, message, stack }, [36mruntime[39m: [31m"browser"[39m|[31m"node"[39m,
    [36msessionId[39m: [31m"..."[39m }

  [38;5;153mv[39m is the schema version so a receiver can handle old clients. [38;5;153msessionId[39m is a random id minted once per page load
  (browser) or per process (Node) — without it you can't stitch a user's records together into a story, which is most of
  what "debug a production issue" means in practice.

  One rule that makes the redaction in Section 2 work: [1m[38;5;153mmsg[39m is always a static string; every dynamic value goes in [38;5;153mctx[39m.[0m
  Interpolating a value into the message smuggles it past a field-level allowlist.

  [1mLevel control.[0m Node reads [38;5;153mLOG_LEVEL[39m from the environment. Browser resolves [38;5;153m?logLevel=debug[39m in the URL first, then
  [38;5;153mlocalStorage.logLevel[39m. Both default to [38;5;153minfo[39m. The query param exists specifically so you can tell a user hitting a
  production bug "add this to your URL and try again" without shipping a new build.

  Does this section look right before I move on to the redaction boundary and the transport?

